# Normalise line endings.
#
# This project is edited from Windows and built inside WSL/Linux.  Without
# this file, a shell script committed from Windows arrives in Linux with CRLF
# line endings and fails as:
#
#     ./tools/bootstrap.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which is one of the least googleable error messages in existence, because
# the offending character (^M) is invisible.  Two lines of config prevent it.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.overlay text eol=lf
*.dts     text eol=lf
*.dtsi    text eol=lf
Makefile  text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch, never diff as text.
*.sr   binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf  binary
